@{ ViewData["Title"] = "Usage terms"; ViewData["Description"] = "The purpose and limits of the firstASPnet educational demonstration."; }
<h1>Usage terms</h1>
<p class="lead">This is an educational demonstration of ASP.NET Core MVC.</p>
<h2>Use fictional details</h2>
<p>The form checks sample input in memory. It does not create records, contact the maintainer or send email. Do not submit personal information, passwords or credentials.</p>
<h2>Understand the limits</h2>
<p>The sample is provided for learning. Its unfinished database, authentication and CRUD exercises remain disabled. It is not a production data-management service.</p>
<h2>Source and questions</h2>
<p>Review the <a href="https://github.com/omarhussainfahmi/ASP.NET-project-Full-dummy-sample-" rel="noopener noreferrer">repository</a> before adapting any code. Existing source and third-party package rights still apply. Use the <a href="/contact">contact page</a> for public project questions, and read how the demo handles input in the <a href="/privacy">privacy page</a>.</p>
